# Nuxt conventions

- `<script setup lang="ts">` with strict TypeScript; typed props and emits.
- Page data via `useFetch` / `useAsyncData` (SSR-safe, deduplicated, unique keys); `$fetch` only in event handlers and server routes. Templates handle `pending`, `error`, and empty results.
- Shared logic in `composables/use*.ts`. Shared state via `useState` or Pinia — never module-level `ref`s, which leak between SSR requests.
- Config through `runtimeConfig`; only non-secrets go under `public`. No `process.env` in app code.
- Auth with a Laravel API: Sanctum SPA cookies (`statefulApi()`, `/sanctum/csrf-cookie` first) or an HttpOnly cookie handled by a server route — never tokens in `localStorage`. During SSR forward cookies with `useRequestHeaders(['cookie'])`.
- Route guards use `defineNuxtRouteMiddleware`; the API still authorizes every request.
- Heavy client-only widgets (charts, editors) go in `<ClientOnly>` or `*.client.vue` and load lazily (`Lazy` component prefix).
- Head and SEO via `useSeoMeta` / `useHead` (`public-site/seo-head.mdc`).
